## Output schema (TypeScript-style)

```ts
{
  seed_state: {
    meta: {turn: 0, model: string, setting_pack: string},
    pc: {name: string, tagline: string, bio: string, stats: {strength: 1-4, dexterity: 1-4, wits: 1-4, lore: 1-4, charisma: 1-4, resolve: 1-4}, conditions: []},
    location: {id: snake_case, name: string, description: string},
    inventory: Array<{id: snake_case, name: string, notes?: string, amount: int}>,  // 1..12 items
    quests: Array<{id: snake_case, title: string, status: "active", objectives: Array<{description: string, done: false, failed: false}>}>,  // ≥1 quest
    scene: {
      tagline: string,
      tags: string[],
      present_npcs: Array<{id: snake_case, name: string, title: string, notes: string, bio: string}>,
      world_state: string[],   // exactly 3 immutable global facts
      recent_events: string[]  // exactly 5 mutable local facts
    },
    compendium: {npcs: {}}      // engine-managed; emit {}
  },
  opening_narrative: string,    // ≥50 chars; 3-4 paragraphs
  actions: [string, string, string, string]  // exactly 4, 7-10 words each
}
```

## Field guidance
- `pc.stats`: six integer values, range 1–4, total 12–18.
- `pc.tagline`: 5–10 words — role + defining trait (e.g. "Structural engineer, nine months sober").
- `pc.bio`: 2–4 sentences — pre-event history, what shaped this person, what they want now.
- `present_npcs[*].bio`: 1–3 sentences of durable identity and motivation.
- `present_npcs[*].notes`: current attitude in this opening scene.
- `scene.world_state`: exactly 3 consolidated global facts — political, economic, infrastructural reality the player would know from living in this setting. Immutable for the entire game. Don't make a separate fact per faction or vocabulary word — consolidate.
- `scene.recent_events`: exactly 5 local facts — specific to this location, these NPCs, this week. Mutable. Each substantial and consequential. Each fact is a plain string — do NOT include category labels or prefixes. Pick distinct categories (one per fact, no two paraphrasing the same truth): faction/power, recent event, infrastructure/resource, local history, key relationships, most recent player action.
- `inventory`: starting items appropriate to PC and scenario. Ranged weapons require a separate ammo stack with a believable starting `amount` (e.g. `{"id": "9mm_rounds", "name": "9mm rounds", "amount": 12}`). Ammo amount is the single source of truth — never put loaded counts in the weapon's `notes`. Melee/single-shot thrown items are exempt. No exotic/legendary weapons at start.
- `opening_narrative`: second person, present tense — exactly 3-4 paragraphs:
  1. Who you are: not biography — one or two sentences grounding the PC in their role and place, with one specific concrete detail.
  2. The local situation right now: drawn directly from the established local facts — what's happening in this specific place this week.
  3. The immediate scene (≥2 paragraphs): drop the player mid-scene with sensory detail. Something is already in motion. The quest tension is implied or beginning to surface — visible in what the player sees and hears, not summarized.
- `actions`: 4 distinct meaningful choices (7-10 words each), valid given the opening situation, each leading in a different direction.
